WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
I am here with the utterly amazing Natalie Portman

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.467
who has written her first children's book,

3
00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:08.080
"Natalie Portman's Fables."

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.980
And joining us to talk about it is our resident reviewer,

5
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.589
none other than Jonah Larson.

6
00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:17.340
(audience cheers and claps)

7
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.302
Hi Jonah.

8
00:00:18.302 --> 00:00:19.150
Hi Drew.

9
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.430
I was so excited to see you again

10
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.710
and I'm really excited to review Ms. Portman's book.

11
00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.930
So nice to meet you.

12
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.420
I'm so impressed by everything you're doing.

13
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.220
Like this is so incredible.

14
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.610
And thank you so much for taking time with the book.

15
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.230
I'm so happy to meet you.

16
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.320
Thank you, Ms. Portman.

17
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.080
I'm really happy that enjoy my work.

18
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.890
It makes me feel really good,

19
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.890
but I enjoyed and loved your book for a plethora of reasons.

20
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.549
You added a classic and modernized twist

21
00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:50.690
to the fables that everyone knows and loves,

22
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.949
like "The Three Little Pigs."

23
00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:56.560
And I've read the book and then my dad read it to me

24
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.760
and then I read it to my little sister Mercy,

25
00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.310
and I loved it more each and every time.

26
00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.550
And my favorite story was "The Three Little Pigs."

27
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.650
And it was also my sister's favorite

28
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.100
because she loved that the big bad Wolf

29
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.140
was a girl because usually in fairy tales,

30
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.339
you think that the female character

31
00:01:15.339 --> 00:01:17.789
always needs to be rescued or isn't as strong,

32
00:01:17.789 --> 00:01:20.070
so she thought it was pretty cool

33
00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.029
to see that the big, bad Wolf was a girl.

34
00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:25.270
But also I just loved the classic messages

35
00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:29.530
of slowing down and taking your time and doing things right,

36
00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.410
and appreciating the things that we sometimes overlook

37
00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.960
and we need to be grateful for like our family,

38
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.520
our friends, and also the earth.

39
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.620
And also wanted to really, I can really relate to you

40
00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.510
and how you brought that special message

41
00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.460
to your mom in the back of your book

42
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.733
because my mom's my favorite too.

43
00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.246
And, for all of those reasons,

44
00:01:52.246 --> 00:01:57.246
I'm rating Ms. Portman's fables five out of five

45
00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.520
crochet loops.

46
00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.170
(Drew claps)
(audience cheers)

47
00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.690 line:15%
Thank you so much.

48
00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.200 line:15%
I am so honored.

49
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.400
I'm like teared up.

50
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.200
This is so meaningful to me that you read it

51
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.290
and took it in that way and processed it.

52
00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.050 line:15%
You're so incredible that you, I don't know,

53
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:18.030 line:15%
the way you express yourself is so impressive too.

54
00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.580
I have to show you Drew something that's so cool.

55
00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.570
Look, it's a Jonah doll.

56
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.850
It looks just like me, we're twins.

57
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.150
And I'm gonna have these on our website as kits.

58
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.850
And, but this one right here, I'm gonna auction

59
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.610
and a 100% of the proceeds are gonna go

60
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:38.790
to my library in Ethiopia, so I'm super excited.

61
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.570
Well, Jonah, can we put that up on our website

62
00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.363
also for your auction?

63
00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:45.733
You would do that?

64
00:02:45.733 --> 00:02:47.563
Thank you so much, Drew.

65
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:50.794
Thank you so much.
Of course.

66
00:02:50.794 --> 00:02:51.978
That's one of the things that we've connected on,

67
00:02:51.978 --> 00:02:54.850
books and helping others and now you're helping me

68
00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:59.080
help other kids so that makes me really happy.

69
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.629
Jonah, this was our plan all along

70
00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:05.380
to take care of people together

71
00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.700
and the love of books being at the forefront.

72
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.690
I love it.

73
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.800
I would be honored.

74
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:12.700
I will help you.

75
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.920
I will be there by your side, whatever I can do.

76
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:15.819
This is your endeavor.

77
00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:18.480
I'm just there to shine a light on it.

78
00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.860
And Natalie, you and Jonah have something in common

79
00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.130
with libraries.

80
00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.860
Will you tell us about the important endeavor

81
00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.010
that you are embarking on?

82
00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:33.010
Yes, I'm doing the National Library Associations' benefit

83
00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.890
coming up, which is so incredible.

84
00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.710
Libraries are of course, one of the,

85
00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:41.459
the model places of community,

86
00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:44.570
one of the last places of community

87
00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.939
in our country and places where people can gather.

88
00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:52.640
People from all different classes, everybody is welcome.

89
00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.820
It's one of the last few public meeting places

90
00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:01.783
and resources of course, cause the books,

91
00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.640
the computers, all of the materials

92
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.300
are available to everybody.

93
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:13.300
And I'm so, so honored to get, to show my respect to them.

94
00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.470
I was talking to everyone here just about

95
00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.200
how much I love your book, Natalie.

96
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.070
And I like you, Jonah, I read it to my daughter.

97
00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:26.100
So it was really nice to hear these famous fables

98
00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.470
that we know so well with a unique spin on it,

99
00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.250
such as the way you so beautifully write them, Natalie.

100
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.140
Thank you.
And this is such

101
00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.930
an elevated, timeless, beautiful children's book

102
00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.660
and it gave me such pleasure reading it as an adult,

103
00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.270
but my children just got so much out of it.

104
00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.260
So thank you for writing it.

105
00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.980
Thank you for putting it out into the world.

106
00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:50.680
Jonah, thank you for reviewing it so thoughtfully.

107
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.760
And Jonah, thank you.

108
00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.850
You are such an incredible young human.

109
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.641
You give me so much hope for the future.

110
00:04:56.641 --> 00:04:58.891
Thank you for what you just said.

111
00:04:58.891 --> 00:05:01.570
I have such respect for you, Natalie Portman.

112
00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.171
I can't even believe I just heard what you said.

113
00:05:03.171 --> 00:05:04.719
Thank you,

114
00:05:04.719 --> 00:05:07.940
Natalie and Jonah, you're both just so wonderful.

115
00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.290
Thank you for letting me be in this space today.

116
00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.947
This is like what the world needs is both of your energies,

117
00:05:13.947 --> 00:05:16.989
"Natalie Portman's Fables" is out now.

